The exports file is created on the machine, it is not part of the image since it
holds the LAN range. Create /etc/exports.d/thomelab.exports with one line per
disk (keep the fsid values when migrating, they are part of the NFS file handles):

/export/thomelab-dynamic-4tb-hdd <lan-cidr>(fsid=<uuid>,rw,no_subtree_check,insecure,root_squash,sync)
/export/thomelab-dynamic-2tb-ssd <lan-cidr>(fsid=<uuid>,rw,no_subtree_check,insecure,root_squash,sync)
/export/thomelab-dynamic-1tb-ssd <lan-cidr>(fsid=<uuid>,rw,no_subtree_check,insecure,root_squash,sync)

Don't add an fsid=0 export of /export: it makes /export the NFSv4 root, so v4
clients would have to mount /thomelab-dynamic-* instead of the full path.

Then run `exportfs -ra`.
